   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Jobs and professions",
     "texto": [
      "To ask what someone does for a living: **Qu'est-ce que tu fais dans la vie ?** (literally «what do you do in life?»).",
      "When you state a job with **être**, the noun usually has no article, unlike in English: **Je suis médecin**, **Elle est professeur**.",
      "Many jobs have a feminine form: **étudiant** → **étudiante**, **infirmier** → **infirmière**, **serveur** → **serveuse**, **vendeur** → **vendeuse**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The plural of «être»",
     "texto": [
      "**Nous** = we. **Ils** = they (masculine). **Elles** = they (feminine).",
      "Many nouns and adjectives form the plural with **-s**; this ending is usually silent: **étudiant** and **étudiants** sound the same.",
      "If a group includes at least one man, you use **ils**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
